Z||000000||fierofreek2001||02-17-2001||11:24 AM||||is the complete front suspension and steering rack rotors, brakes, calipers, cross member, etc.  the same between an 86 se v6, and an 87 4cyl coupe ?<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||02-17-2001||01:02 PM||||Everything but the springs. I used a complete '85 V6 suspension,crossmember and all, for my '87 coupe project. The springs have different rates but I couldn't tell a difference driving it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPBody||02-17-2001||07:47 PM||||The entire assembly should interchange, although springs may have different stiffness.  Cars with WS6 option will have a quicker steering rack.  Check RPO sticker in front compartment on left fender well for option codes.<BR>||||reg||1
